## INT-204: Tool Contract + NLQ API Server

**Goal:** One tool interface for OpenAI function calling and Claude tool use.
Tools wrap existing `QueryRouter` methods -- no new execution surface.

INT-204 defines ALL shared types so it compiles and passes clippy/tests alone.
INT-203 only adds the LLM implementation.

### Types defined in INT-204

**New file: `neumann_server/src/nlq_api/mod.rs`**

All shared types live here so INT-204 is self-contained:

```rust
/// Configuration for the NLQ gateway (provider/model settings).
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct NlqConfig {
    pub provider: String,     // "openai" | "anthropic"
    pub api_key: String,
    pub model: String,
    pub max_tokens: u32,      // default 2048
    pub temperature: f32,     // default 0.0
    pub max_rounds: u32,      // default 5
}

/// Trait for NLQ planners. INT-203 provides the implementation.
#[async_trait]
pub trait NlqPlan: Send + Sync {
    async fn plan(&self, question: &str, ctx: &NlqApiContext) -> Result<NlqResponse, NlqApiError>;
}

/// Response from the NLQ gateway.
#[derive(Debug, Serialize)]
pub struct NlqResponse {
    pub query: Option<String>,
    pub result_type: String,
    pub result: Vec<serde_json::Value>,
    pub answer: Option<String>,
    pub error: Option<String>,
}

/// NLQ API error type (wraps ApiError for HTTP responses).
#[derive(Debug)]
pub struct NlqApiError(pub ApiError);
impl From<ApiError> for NlqApiError { ... }
impl IntoResponse for NlqApiError { ... }

pub struct NlqApiContext {
    pub router: Arc<parking_lot::RwLock<QueryRouter>>,
